# Packaging output (.deb + its checksum + the artifact-bound preflight guard).
# Ignored so a build cannot dirty its own tree and make the NEXT build refuse.
/dist
/build-pkg

# CMake out-of-source build dirs
/build
/build-*
/out
/cmake-build-*

# Runtime SQLite store (created next to the executable)
denso.db
denso.db-shm
denso.db-wal

# Screenshots / generated images (assets/icon.png is force-tracked)
*.png

# ONNX Runtime binaries (provisioned per platform, not tracked)
third_party/onnxruntime/

# CUDA execution-provider runtime DLLs (TensorRT + cuDNN), provisioned locally
# and copied beside the exe at build time — see docs/GPU_SETUP.md. Not tracked.
third_party/gpu_ep/

# TensorRT engines + their class-name sidecars + the ORT TensorRT-EP engine
# cache — all built locally and specific to the GPU architecture and TensorRT
# version, so never tracked. The .names.json is generated ON-DEVICE beside its
# engine (TRT plans carry no name metadata), so it is exactly as untrackable as
# the engine: leaving it unignored made every Jetson checkout permanently dirty,
# which tools/build_package.sh correctly refuses to package.
models/*.engine
models/*.names.json
models/trt_cache/

# Local scratch + MODEL ARTIFACTS. Ignore them by PATTERN, not by name: naming
# `models/digitv2.onnx` specifically meant every NEW model (digitv3.onnx, a .pt
# checkpoint) landed untracked-and-unignored, permanently dirtying the tree — and
# tools/build_package.sh then refuses to package a dirty tree, so a new model
# blocked the build until someone noticed. That happened for .names.json too.
#
# denso.onnx stays TRACKED (committed before this rule; gitignore does not untrack
# an already-tracked file). Everything else under models/ is a build/training
# artifact: .onnx exports, .pt checkpoints, TRT engines, sidecars, the cache.
note.txt
models/*.onnx
models/*.pt
models/digitv2.engine.bak
